   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Cropland Abandonment in Yiyang</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">Cropland Abandonment in Yiyang</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">China: Long-Term Landsat-Based Mapping and Regional Association Analysis</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">China: Long-Term Landsat-Based Mapping and Regional Association Analysis</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <dc:subject>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>cropland abandonment; Landsat time series; moving window; plain--hill transition; XGBoost; SHAP; spatial heterogeneity</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:subject>
   <dc:type>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>Text</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:type>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Annual monitoring of cropland abandonment supports targeted cropland management. Consistent event definitions</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">Annual monitoring of cropland abandonment supports targeted cropland management. Consistent event definitions</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">denominators and spatial support enable comparisons across regions and periods. This study aims to characterize annual land-cover transitions that serve as a proxy for new cropland abandonment in Yiyang</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">denominators and spatial support enable comparisons across regions and periods. This study aims to characterize annual land-cover transitions that serve as a proxy for new cropland abandonment in Yiyang</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">China</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">China</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and to compare their spatial associations between the plain and hilly regions. Random forest classification provides annual 30 m Landsat land use and land cover (LULC) maps for 2010--2025. An operational three-year rule identifies cropland in the preceding year followed by forest or grassland in two consecutive years. Annual mapped event area is divided by preceding-year cropland area. Long-term grid responses average valid annual rates</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and to compare their spatial associations between the plain and hilly regions. Random forest classification provides annual 30 m Landsat land use and land cover (LULC) maps for 2010--2025. An operational three-year rule identifies cropland in the preceding year followed by forest or grassland in two consecutive years. Annual mapped event area is divided by preceding-year cropland area. Long-term grid responses average valid annual rates</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and spatially blocked XGBoost--SHAP models retain 6302 grids and 19 predictors. During the period of 2012--2024</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and spatially blocked XGBoost--SHAP models retain 6302 grids and 19 predictors. During the period of 2012--2024</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">mean annual mapped event area is 104.60 kmÂ²</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">mean annual mapped event area is 104.60 kmÂ²</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and the mean annual mapped event rate is 2.31. Mean mapped event rates are 6.00 in the hilly region and 1.41 in the plain region</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and the mean annual mapped event rate is 2.31. Mean mapped event rates are 6.00 in the hilly region and 1.41 in the plain region</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">with respective peaks in 2015 and 2020. Citywide</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">with respective peaks in 2015 and 2020. Citywide</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">plain-region and hilly-region holdout RÂ² values are 0.744</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">plain-region and hilly-region holdout RÂ² values are 0.744</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">0.672 and 0.589</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">0.672 and 0.589</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">and AUCs for relatively high-rate grids are 0.957</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">and AUCs for relatively high-rate grids are 0.957</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">0.913 and 0.880. Elevation accounts for 38.06 of citywide relative SHAP importance; mean cropland patch area and fragmentation index together account for 35.39 in the hilly region. A same-cohort 2021 comparison shows response-period sensitivity in predictor rankings. These mapped transitions highlight region-specific associations that can guide field checks; land-use records are needed to distinguish the cessation of cultivation from intentional woody-cover conversion.</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="en-US">0.913 and 0.880. Elevation accounts for 38.06 of citywide relative SHAP importance; mean cropland patch area and fragmentation index together account for 35.39 in the hilly region. A same-cohort 2021 comparison shows response-period sensitivity in predictor rankings. These mapped transitions highlight region-specific associations that can guide field checks; land-use records are needed to distinguish the cessation of cultivation from intentional woody-cover conversion.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
